---
title: Ginger Shakin' Beef
course: Main
servings: 2
locale: en
difficulty: Easy
---

Remove and finely slice the @sirloin steak, 1.5 cm thick{300%g}'s fat. Place it in a cold frying pan over a medium-high heat to crisp up. Add the @ginger{4%cm}(peeled and matchsticked) to crisp up too.

Dice the steak into 3 cm chunks and toss with the @miso paste{1%tbsp} until well coated.

Scoop the crispy fat and ginger out and set aside. Add the steak chunks to the pan. Cook for ~{4%minutes}, tossing regularly. Drizzle in the @runny honey{2%tsp} and @red wine vinegar{1%tbsp}. Toss for ~{1%minute} more until shiny and sticky.

Meanwhile, halve the @pak choi{2}(250 g), cook in a pan of boiling water for just 1 minute so they retain a bit of crunch, then drain well and plate up.

Spoon over the steak and sticky juices from the pan, and finish with the reserved crispy bits.